<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak August key M2 money up 19.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Slovak August key M2 money up 19.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) on Friday said its key money supply measure, M2, was up 19.5 percent year-on-year in August, compared with a 20.1 percent rise in August 1995.  </p>
<p> SLOVAK MONEY SUPPLY    Aug '96    July '96   Aug '95</p>
<p>M2 overall</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	  +19.5	+21.0	+20.1</p>
<p>pct change</p>
<p>  as of Jan 1		 +5.3	 +4.1	 +6.85</p>
<p>Note. M2 measures currency, demand and time deposits, savings deposits, and foreign currency deposits.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsrsoom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
</text>
